From 59bc7252e434fb554ce59b6e746f9311875e6cb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:55:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] test(emitter): witness the source-file owner of undecorated
 computed-property hoists

The prepared undecorated-outer-property-hoist family reaches the named
evaluation hoist only inside a function body. tsc's `visitEachChild(SourceFile)`
runs the same hoist through visitLexicalEnvironment and mergeLexicalEnvironment
(after prologue directives), which the Rust transform's source-file visit does
not own. Adds the `source-followup-top-level` group (18 complete commands: the
top-level class, the same file behind a `"use strict"` prologue, and the
decorated control) with fresh TypeScript 6.0.3 observations (twice each,
diagnostic-free), registers it in the witness harness, and records the Rust
baselines on the cause-2 production: in-function family 1 exact / 5 failed,
top-level group 8 exact / 10 failed (both undecorated sources on the five
lowered configurations), same failure shape as the prepared family.

Receipts: ratchets/h2-8a-decorator-followup-cause3-baseline.v1.json,
ratchets/h2-8a-decorator-followup-top-level-baseline.v1.json. The prepared 48
inputs and observations are unchanged.
